B3B3" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(2.35,0)"><path d="M -2.08 -2.77 h 4.15 v 11.07 h -4.15 Z M 6.23 -2.77 h 4.15 v 8.3 h -4.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 13.01 0) translate(32.48,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -29.71 -3.77)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="60.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F3.pic1.25" class="ltx_text">Backward</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>RL computation times on one of the test problems.
Error bars indicate 2<math id="S4.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> confidence intervals. Each backward pass also includes one forward pass (to evaluate the inputs of Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3.4 Additional Implementation Details and Properties of DiffMPC ‣ 3 Differentiable Model Predictive Control on the GPU ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Warm-starting.</span>
Using <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span>’s PCG routine for solving the KKT systems enables warm-starting both the forward and backward passes.
Figure <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ B.1 Reinforcement Learning Benchmark ‣ Appendix B Results: Additional Details and Experiments ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> in the appendix reports speedups from warm-starting, computed as the ratio <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\textrm{cold}-\textrm{warm}}{\textrm{cold}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mtext>cold</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext>warm</mtext></mrow><mtext>cold</mtext></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\textrm{cold}-\textrm{warm}}{\textrm{cold}}</annotation></semantics></math> comparing the RL computation times using <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span> and of <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span> with zero initial guesses provided to PCG.
For the PCG exit tolerance <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-12}</annotation></semantics></math> that is used in this section’s results, warm-starting gives modest speedups of
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\%</annotation></semantics></math> for both the forward and backward passes.
These speedups increase to
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11\%</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9\%</annotation></semantics></math> for the forward and backward passes, respectively, if the tolerance is set to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we expect additional speedups for low tolerances and in applications where <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span> is used to replan at high frequencies.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Timing Results for Imitation Learning</h3>

