<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Solver: Additional Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Vector-Jacobian products (VJPs) vs Jacobian-vector products (JVPs)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 A Primer on Differentiable Optimization ‣ 2 Background on Differentiable Optimization ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), vector-Jacobian products (VJP) for computing gradients of scalar-valued functions of solutions to optimization problems can be computed as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial w}{\partial\theta}^{\top}v=-\frac{\partial F}{\partial\theta}^{\top}\left[\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}\right]^{-1}v=-\frac{\partial F}{\partial\theta}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{z}\\
\widetilde{\lambda}\end{bmatrix},\quad\text{where $\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{z}\\
\widetilde{\lambda}\end{bmatrix}$ solves}\underbrace{\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}}_{(n+q)\times(n+q)}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{z}\\
\widetilde{\lambda}\end{bmatrix}}_{(n+q)}=\underbrace{v}_{(n+q)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mtext> solves</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial w}{\partial\theta}^{\top}v=-\frac{\partial F}{\partial\theta}^{\top}\left[\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}\right]^{-1}v=-\frac{\partial F}{\partial\theta}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{z}\\
\widetilde{\lambda}\end{bmatrix},\quad\text{where $\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{z}\\
\widetilde{\lambda}\end{bmatrix}$ solves}\underbrace{\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}}_{(n+q)\times(n+q)}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{z}\\
\widetilde{\lambda}\end{bmatrix}}_{(n+q)}=\underbrace{v}_{(n+q)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+q)\times(n+q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+q)\times(n+q)}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{z},\widetilde{\lambda})\in\mathbb{R}^{n+q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{z},\widetilde{\lambda})\in\mathbb{R}^{n+q}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{n+q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{n+q}</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, computing JVPs of the form <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial w}{\partial\theta}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial w}{\partial\theta}v</annotation></semantics></math> requires computing the full Jacobian <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial z}{\partial\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial z}{\partial\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the solution to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> linear systems. Indeed, by (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 A Primer on Differentiable Optimization ‣ 2 Background on Differentiable Optimization ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), each sensitivity <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial z}{\partial\theta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial z}{\partial\theta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by solving</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}\begin{bmatrix}\frac{\partial z}{\partial\theta_{i}}\\[2.84526pt]
\frac{\partial\lambda}{\partial\theta_{i}}\end{bmatrix}=-\frac{\partial F}{\partial\theta_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial F}{\partial w}\begin{bmatrix}\frac{\partial z}{\partial\theta_{i}}\\[2.84526pt]
\frac{\partial\lambda}{\partial\theta_{i}}\end{bmatrix}=-\frac{\partial F}{\partial\theta_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, reverse mode differentiation via VJPs is preferred to forward mode differentiation via JVPs in many applications, such as reinforcement learning and imitation learning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>PCG Algorithm</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Projected Conjugate Gradient (PCG) algorithm introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Adabag et al., 2024</a>)</cite> is used to solve the linear KKT systems in <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span> (see Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ A.3 Line search ‣ Appendix A Solver: Additional Details ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
Note that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.3 Solving the Linear Systems while Leveraging Parallelism ‣ 3 Differentiable Model Predictive Control on the GPU ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) takes the form</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=d+(Q_{0}^{-1}q_{0},\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1},\dots,\zeta_{T-1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=d+(Q_{0}^{-1}q_{0},\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1},\dots,\zeta_{T-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{t}=A_{t}Q_{t}^{-1}q_{t}+B_{t}R_{t}^{-1}r_{t}+A_{k}^{+}Q_{t+1}^{-1}q_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{t}=A_{t}Q_{t}^{-1}q_{t}+B_{t}R_{t}^{-1}r_{t}+A_{k}^{+}Q_{t+1}^{-1}q_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, lines 1, 2, 6, and 11 of Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ A.3 Line search ‣ Appendix A Solver: Additional Details ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> are parallelized over time, reducing computation times when executed on the GPU.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Line search</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After solving each <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QP</span>, we use a standard line search method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nocedal &amp; Wright, 2006</a>, Algorithm 18.3)</cite> described next. Below, we denote by <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{+}=(x^{+},u^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{+}=(x^{+},u^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> the solution to <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QP</span>, which is evaluated at <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math>. The objective of the line search is to select an appropriate step size <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> so the new solution <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x+\alpha(x^{+}-x),u+\alpha(u^{+}-u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x+\alpha(x^{+}-x),u+\alpha(u^{+}-u))</annotation></semantics></math> is closer to an optimal solution to <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OCP</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The line search uses a merit function <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> defined as the weighted sum of the cost and constraints</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x,u):=\sum_{t}\left(c^{x}_{t}(x_{t})+c^{u}_{t}(u_{t})+\mu\left\|f(x_{t+1},x_{t},u_{t})\right\|_{1}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x,u):=\sum_{t}\left(c^{x}_{t}(x_{t})+c^{u}_{t}(u_{t})+\mu\left\|f(x_{t+1},x_{t},u_{t})\right\|_{1}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where
the penalty parameter <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is set as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nocedal &amp; Wright, 2006</a>, Equation 18.33 with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{\sum_{t}\nabla c^{x}_{t}(x_{t})^{\top}(x_{t}^{+}-x_{t})+\nabla c^{u}_{t}(u_{t})^{\top}(u^{+}_{t}-u_{t})}{0.5\sum_{t}\|f(x_{t+1},x_{t},u_{t})\|_{1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{\sum_{t}\nabla c^{x}_{t}(x_{t})^{\top}(x_{t}^{+}-x_{t})+\nabla c^{u}_{t}(u_{t})^{\top}(u^{+}_{t}-u_{t})}{0.5\sum_{t}\|f(x_{t+1},x_{t},u_{t})\|_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The decrease condition for accepting a step size <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nocedal &amp; Wright, 2006</a>, Equation 18.28)</cite></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\varphi_{\alpha}:=\varphi(x+\alpha\Delta x,u+\alpha\Delta u)-\varphi(x,u)-\eta\alpha D_{\mu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\varphi_{\alpha}:=\varphi(x+\alpha\Delta x,u+\alpha\Delta u)-\varphi(x,u)-\eta\alpha D_{\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> (we use <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0.4</annotation></semantics></math>), with descent direction defined as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nocedal &amp; Wright, 2006</a>, Equation 18.29)</cite></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mu}=\sum_{t}\nabla c^{x}_{t}(x_{t})^{\top}(x_{t}^{+}-x_{t})+\nabla c^{u}_{t}(u_{t})^{\top}(u^{+}_{t}-u_{t})-\mu\|f(x_{t+1},x_{t},u_{t})\|_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mu}=\sum_{t}\nabla c^{x}_{t}(x_{t})^{\top}(x_{t}^{+}-x_{t})+\nabla c^{u}_{t}(u_{t})^{\top}(u^{+}_{t}-u_{t})-\mu\|f(x_{t+1},x_{t},u_{t})\|_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Merit function values
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x+\alpha\Delta x,u+\alpha\Delta u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x+\alpha\Delta x,u+\alpha\Delta u)</annotation></semantics></math>
are evaluated in parallel over different pre-defined step sizes in decreasing order <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}:=\{1.0,0.7,0.3,0.1,0.01\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:4.0pt;height:3.1pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="2.4pt" width="4.0pt"><mo mathsize="0.700em">↘</mo></mpadded></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}:=\{1.0,0.7,0.3,0.1,0.01\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The line search method is described in further details in Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ A.3 Line search ‣ Appendix A Solver: Additional Details ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:186.8pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> PCG for solving <math id="alg3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\lambda=\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\lambda=\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.3 Solving the Linear Systems while Leveraging Parallelism ‣ 3 Differentiable Model Predictive Control on the GPU ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Adabag et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg3.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inputs</span>:
<math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S,\gamma,\Phi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S,\gamma,\Phi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
initial guess <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, tolerance <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            
</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\gamma-S\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\gamma-S\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg3.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"><math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="alg3.l3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{t}=\gamma_{t}-S_{t}\lambda_{t-1:t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#B3B3B3" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}=\gamma_{t}-S_{t}\lambda_{t-1:t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="alg3.l3.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}=\Phi^{-1}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}=\Phi^{-1}r</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg3.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"><math id="alg3.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="alg3.l4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{r}_{t}=\Phi^{-1}_{t}r_{t-1:t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#B3B3B3" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{t}=\Phi^{-1}_{t}r_{t-1:t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="alg3.l4.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=r^{\top}\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=r^{\top}\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=Sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=Sp</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg3.l8.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"><math id="alg3.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="alg3.l8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{t}=S_{t}p_{t-1:t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#B3B3B3" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}=S_{t}p_{t-1:t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="alg3.l8.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=p^{\top}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=p^{\top}y</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\eta/v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\eta/v</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\lambda+\alpha p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\lambda+\alpha p</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r-\alpha y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r-\alpha y</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}=\Phi^{-1}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}=\Phi^{-1}r</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg3.l13.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"><math id="alg3.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l13.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="alg3.l13.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{r}_{t}=\Phi^{-1}_{t}r_{t-1:t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#B3B3B3" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;" mathcolor="#B3B3B3">1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{t}=\Phi^{-1}_{t}r_{t-1:t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="alg3.l13.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{\prime}=r^{\top}\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{\prime}=r^{\top}\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\eta^{\prime}/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\eta^{\prime}/\eta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\tilde{r}+\beta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\tilde{r}+\beta p</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\eta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\eta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>: solution <math id="alg3.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> to the system <math id="alg3.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\lambda=\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\lambda=\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:194.8pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> Linesearch for SQP.</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg4.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inputs</span>:
Previous solution <math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math> for formulating <span id="alg4.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QP</span>, <span id="alg4.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom"><span style="visibility:hidden"><math id="alg4.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:4.0pt;height:3.1pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="2.4pt" width="4.0pt"><mo mathsize="0.700em">↘</mo></mpadded></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
solution <math id="alg4.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{+}=(x^{+},u^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{+}=(x^{+},u^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> to <span id="alg4.l1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QP</span>,
candidate step sizes <math id="alg4.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}=\{1.0,0.7,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:4.0pt;height:3.1pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="2.4pt" width="4.0pt"><mo mathsize="0.700em">↘</mo></mpadded></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}=\{1.0,0.7,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            
</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            Evaluate merit function <math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"> Eq. <a href="#A1.E15" title="In A.3 Line search ‣ Appendix A Solver: Additional Details ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a><span id="alg4.l3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            Evaluate penalty parameter <math id="alg4.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"> Eq. <a href="#A1.E16" title="In A.3 Line search ‣ Appendix A Solver: Additional Details ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a><span id="alg4.l4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            Evaluate descent direction <math id="alg4.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"> Eq. <a href="#A1.E18" title="In A.3 Line search ‣ Appendix A Solver: Additional Details ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a><span id="alg4.l5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:4.0pt;height:3.1pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="2.4pt" width="4.0pt"><mo mathsize="0.700em">↘</mo></mpadded></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
<span id="alg4.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"> in parallel<span id="alg4.l6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              Evaluate decrease
condition
<math id="alg4.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\varphi_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\varphi_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg4.l7.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"> Eq. <a href="#A1.E17" title="In A.3 Line search ‣ Appendix A Solver: Additional Details ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a><span id="alg4.l7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg4.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leftarrow\min(\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:4.0pt;height:3.1pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="2.4pt" width="4.0pt"><mo mathsize="0.700em">↘</mo></mpadded></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leftarrow\min(\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\alpha}\in\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:4.0pt;height:3.1pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="2.4pt" width="4.0pt"><mo mathsize="0.700em">↘</mo></mpadded></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\alpha}\in\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
<span id="alg4.l9.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"> sequentially<span id="alg4.l9.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg4.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\varphi_{\widetilde{\alpha}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\varphi_{\widetilde{\alpha}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg4.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leftarrow\widetilde{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leftarrow\widetilde{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg4.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;float:right;"> select largest step size<span id="alg4.l11.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
               Break
  
</div>
<div id="alg4.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return</span>: New solution <math id="alg4.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x+\alpha(x^{+}-x),u+\alpha(u^{+}-u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x+\alpha(x^{+}-x),u+\alpha(u^{+}-u))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Results: Additional Details and Experiments</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\sim\mathcal{N}(\bar{y},\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\sim\mathcal{N}(\bar{y},\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a Gaussian random variable with mean <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance matrix <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\sim\mathcal{U}([a,b])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\sim\mathcal{U}([a,b])</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a uniform random variable in the interval <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Reinforcement Learning Benchmark</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the RL benchmark, we start by describing the solvers used and how they were modified to produce a fair comparison of <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Theseus</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mpc.pytorch</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">trajax</span>, and <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span>. We then consider a linear problem to facilitate ablations on the problem size and study the impact of warm starting on the PCG algorithm. Finally, we consider a nonlinear spacecraft example where we compare the computation times for <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">trajax</span> and <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T1" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:30%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Computation times (s) with
<span id="A2.T1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mpc.pytorch</span> for Problem 1 on the GPU.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T1.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T1.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T1.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;"> Pass</th>
<th id="A2.T1.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;">Original</th>
<th id="A2.T1.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;">Modified</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T1.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T1.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;">Fwd</th>
<td id="A2.T1.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;"><math id="A2.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="67.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>67.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">67.9</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T1.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;"><math id="A2.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1.9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">1.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1.9}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T1.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T1.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;">Bwd</th>
<td id="A2.T1.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;"><math id="A2.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="136.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>136.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">136.4</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T1.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.5pt 1.9pt;"><math id="A2.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{4.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">4.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{4.5}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup.</span> For this RL benchmark, we use an evaluation scheme similar to the RL pipeline in Fig. <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5 Application to domain randomization for driving at the limits ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. All methods use compute gradients via implicit differentiation and use float64 precision. Timing is conducted on a workstation with a 64-Core AMD Threadripper 3990X CPU and a NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 GPU running Ubuntu 22.04. For these evaluations on <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QP</span> problems, <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mpc.pytorch</span> is constrained to 1 iLQR iteration, the line search is disabled, and flags are set so that it exits after the first iteration without detaching gradients. The original code is slightly modified to eliminate a serial list comprehension that causes the library to scale poorly when inequality constraints are disabled. Table <a href="#A2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ B.1 Reinforcement Learning Benchmark ‣ Appendix B Results: Additional Details and Experiments ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> compares our modified version of <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mpc.pytorch</span> to the base version on the first seed from problem 1, and shows that our modifications reduce the solve times of the forward pass and gradient computations.
Since <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Theseus</span> only supports unconstrained non-linear least-square optimization problems, the dynamics are rolled out in the objective function as done in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wan et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. The damped least squares method is used and constrained to 1 iteration of the dense Cholesky solver.
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Trajax</span> uses the in-built iLQR <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OCP</span> solver, and is constrained to 1 iLQR iteration and a minimum line search step of 0.99 (we found that a minimum of 1 prevents any solution from being accepted). The <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tvlqr</span> method is used for the backward pass.
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span> is also limited to 1 <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QP</span> solve and 1 line search iteration, with <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}=\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:4.0pt;height:3.1pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="2.4pt" width="4.0pt"><mo mathsize="0.700em">↘</mo></mpadded></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{{\scalebox{0.5}{$\searrow$}}}{\alpha}=\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The underlying PCG solver uses an exit tolerance of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-12}</annotation></semantics></math> for both the forwards and backwards passes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QP problems.</span> We consider the six problems defined in Table <a href="#A2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ B.1 Reinforcement Learning Benchmark ‣ Appendix B Results: Additional Details and Experiments ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The dynamics of each problem are defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}=Ax_{t}+Bu_{t}+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}=Ax_{t}+Bu_{t}+b</annotation></semantics></math>. The dynamics matrix <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is randomized according to <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=I+0.1\Delta A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=I+0.1\Delta A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{vec}(\Delta A)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{vec}(\Delta A)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and its eigenvalues are clipped to lie within the unit circle so that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda(A)|\in(0,0.99]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda(A)|\in(0,0.99]</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, we let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{vec}(B)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{vec}(B)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.10^{-4}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mn>0.10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.10^{-4}I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and sample initial conditions as <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,25I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,25I)</annotation></semantics></math>. The cost functions in <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OCP</span> are quadratic functions <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}^{x,\theta}(x)=x^{\top}Qx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}^{x,\theta}(x)=x^{\top}Qx</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}^{u,\theta}(u)=\|u\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}^{u,\theta}(u)=\|u\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The RL reward is defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x,u)=-(\|x\|_{2}^{2}+\|u\|_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,u)=-(\|x\|_{2}^{2}+\|u\|_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. The parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> that are optimized are <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\text{diag}(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\text{diag}(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>. For each of these problems, we compute statistics over ten independent runs per method, as we observed little variation in computation times within each problem (apart from <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Theseus</span> on the CPU). Timing results are in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.1 Reinforcement Learning Benchmark ‣ Appendix B Results: Additional Details and Experiments ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The results of Problem 1 are illustrated in Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.1 Timing Results for Reinforcement Learning ‣ 4 Results: Faster Solves and Learning on the GPU ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, and are representative of performance across the tested problem instances.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T2" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Parameters in the RL benchmark: state dimension <math id="A2.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, control dimension <math id="A2.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, MPC horizon <math id="A2.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, RL episodes length <math id="A2.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="A2.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Problem</th>
<th id="A2.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A2.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
