<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Warm-starting.</span> We provide further results in Figure <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ B.1 Reinforcement Learning Benchmark ‣ Appendix B Results: Additional Details and Experiments ‣ Differentiable Model Predictive Controlon the GPU" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> to assess the benefits from warm-starting <span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span> for different PCG exit tolerances <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\{10^{-4},10^{-8},10^{-12}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\{10^{-4},10^{-8},10^{-12}\}</annotation></semantics></math> on Problem 1.
Statistics are computed over <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> independent runs for each PCG exit tolerance. We observe speedups for both the forward and backward passes. Speedups are more significant for lower PCG exit tolerances <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. We note that tolerances in the order <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> are reasonable for many applications, see the results in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Adabag et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. To ensure fair comparisons against baselines, we used the lowest tolerance <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-12}</annotation></semantics></math> in all other results in the paper, and anticipate that additional speedups compared to these baselines could be observed by selecting a smaller exit tolerance <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06179v1/figs/speedup_warm_start.png" id="A2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/137;" width="548" height="137" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>RL with <span id="A2.F9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiffMPC</span>: Speedups from warm-starting <math id="A2.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\textrm{SolveTime}_{\textrm{cold}}-\textrm{SolveTime}_{\textrm{warm}}}{\textrm{SolveTime}_{\textrm{cold}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>SolveTime</mtext><mtext>cold</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mtext>SolveTime</mtext><mtext>warm</mtext></msub></mrow><msub><mtext>SolveTime</mtext><mtext>cold</mtext></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\textrm{SolveTime}_{\textrm{cold}}-\textrm{SolveTime}_{\textrm{warm}}}{\textrm{SolveTime}_{\textrm{cold}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for different PCG exit tolerances <math id="A2.F9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A2.F9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 2</annotation></semantics></math> standard deviation intervals.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Timing results on CPU and GPU across 6 problem instances with mean time and <math id="A2.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> (s).</figcaption>
